/-!
# Magic Square winning implications

This module proves the exact induced Magic Square value and variable
consistency bounds on anticommuting Pauli tuples.

## References

The Magic Square value and consistency theorems prove items 6 and 7
of `lem:qld-win-implications`
from `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:192-267`
and blueprint `lem:qld-win-implications` and `lem:qld-win-implications-obs`.
-/



open scoped BigOperators Matrix ComplexOrder

open MIPStarRE.QPBT

open LIDT.MIPStarRE.LDT hiding Measurement
open LIDT.MIPStarRE.Quantum



open MIPStarRE.QPBT.WinImplications

theorem MIPStarRE.QPBT.WinImplications.gatedMsRejection_le_fixedEdge {P : _root_.MIPStarRE.QPBT.AdmissibleParams} {ε : ℝ}
    (S : _root_.MIPStarRE.QPBT.ProjectiveSetting P ε) (xy : _root_.MIPStarRE.QPBT.MsType × _root_.MIPStarRE.QPBT.MsType)
    (hxy : xy ∈ (_root_.MIPStarRE.QPBT.graphDistribution _root_.MIPStarRE.QPBT.msEdges _root_.MIPStarRE.QPBT.msEdges_nonempty).support) :
    _root_.LIDT.MIPStarRE.LDT.avgOver (_root_.LIDT.MIPStarRE.LDT.uniformDistribution (_root_.MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliTuple P)) (fun ω =>
        if _root_.MIPStarRE.QPBT.IsAnticommuting ω then _root_.MIPStarRE.QPBT.WinImplications.inducedMsRejection S ω xy else 0) ≤
      (Fintype.card _root_.MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliEdge : ℝ) * ε := by sorry
